This project is an independent reimplementation of the idea behind the `shunt`
plugin in Spotify's portal-ai-plugins:

    https://github.com/spotify/portal-ai-plugins/tree/main/plugins/shunt
    Copyright Spotify AB, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Spotify's design - a PreToolUse hook that blocks large reads and routes them to
a cheaper model, paired with skills that tell the orchestrator what to do
instead - is the origin of this approach, and the eval-case structure here
follows theirs.

No Spotify source code is copied. The worker transport differs entirely:
Spotify's routes through portal-cli to Spotify Portal/AiKA, while this project
uses a native Claude Code subagent pinned to Haiku and has no third-party
dependency.
